    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <FlexiPage> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading "unable to find
         matching parent xml file" error.

         =====================================================================
         🔴 2026-08-27 - "ADVANCE STAGE" REPLACED BY NAMED PER-HOP BUTTONS. USER DECISION: "we
         don't need a quick action named 'Advance Stage'; instead we need the NEXT STAGE NAME."
         Finishes the wave a939e97 (2026-08-26) started on the disposition NDA/LOI/PSA pages;
         Underwriting__c carries no record types, so this page has a single sequence, not a
         disposition/acquisition split.
         =====================================================================

         Underwriting__c.Advance_Stage is REMOVED (not amended) and replaced by two pure-AND
         entries: Move_to_In_Progress (Requested -> In Progress) and Move_to_Completed
         (Approved -> Completed). See each entry's own comment below for why this ALSO fixes a
         live latent defect (the removed entry's booleanFilter '1 AND (2 OR 3)' is measured to be
         ignored by the renderer) and why In Progress -> Approved deliberately gets no button
         (owned by Underwriting__c.Submit_for_Approval / the approval process).

         ⚠ STILL NOT PROVEN, AND NOT PROVABLE FROM A REPO: RENDERER BEHAVIOUR. After deploying, a
         human must open an Underwriting record at 'In Progress' and confirm ONLY
         'Submit for Approval' shows — no stage button, no hint text — because that is the check
         that distinguishes this fix from the OR-defect it replaces. See
         agent-output/design-requirements.md §7.2.

         =====================================================================
         🔴 2026-08-28 — force:relatedListContainer ADDED TO THE header REGION (identifier
         relatedLists, alongside highlightsPanel). HALF OF A TWO-FILE APPROVAL-HISTORY FIX; see
         layouts/Underwriting__c-Underwriting Layout.layout-meta.xml's own comment for the other
         half and why NEITHER WORKS ALONE. Needed because
         approvalProcesses/Underwriting__c.Underwriting_Approval (new) locks this record
         (recordEditability = AdminOnly) while pending — without a visible Recall route a
         mis-submitted record is stuck. Placed in header, next to highlightsPanel, so it is
         visible without a tab click, matching the Disposition_Record_Page precedent.
         🔴 BEFORE EDITING THIS FILE AGAIN: this page was deployed today (2026-08-28,
         retrieve-diffed against the org via a target metadata dir retrieve before this edit —
         zero structural drift found). Repeat that check, not a plain `sf project retrieve`,
         which strips this whole comment block on every prior page it has touched.
         ===================================================================== -->
